<title>RUSSIA: Russian c. bank sets VSM new bond coupon 56.14 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian c. bank sets VSM new bond coupon 56.14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's central bank set the first coupon of a new RAO Vysokoskorostnye Magistrali (VSM) one-year bond to be issued on October 3 at 14,151 roubles, or 56.14 percent at an annual rate, the bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Full details of the issue:</p>
<p>    Issue volume			 240 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			100,000 rbls</p>
<p>    Tenor				  365 days</p>
<p>    First coupon			 56.14 pct</p>
<p>    First coupon payment date	Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p>    Second coupon payment date     April 3, 1997</p>
<p>    Third coupon payment date	July 3, 1997</p>
<p>    Fourth coupon payment date     October 10, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date			October 3, 1997</p>
<p>State-owned VSM (High-Speed Railways in English) is building a high-speed rail link between Moscow and St Petersburg.</p>
<p>It issued 120 billion of government-backed bonds at the beginning of this year.</p>
<p>The securities are effectively the same as Russian OFZ interest-bearing government bonds. OFZ bonds pay quarterly interest linked to current issues of GKO discount Treasury bills.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
